HOLD IT RIGHT THERE! This is not an option. Holding the Amulet of
Yendor blocks level teleports, so unless you have about 40 cursed
potions of gain level on you, you can't do that. Unless you meant just
using regular teleports to get from the down staircase to the up
staircase. In that case, go for it, but you'd better have a lot of
wands and an RoTC. Don't forget that the amulet also blocks inter-
level teleports 1/3 of the time, so don't put too much faith in one
zap.

As for what to use the scrolls on... If you have a magic lamp, don't
waste them on Sunsword or Snickersnee. Either ditch them, or bury them
in your bag of holding (which you do have, right?) for bonus points.
Excalibur isn't a bad choice because of the autosearching and drain
resistance, but it's not the best in terms of damage. If you already
have drain resistance in some form, this isn't entirely necessary, but
keep Excalibur around so that you can more easily find the portals
once you get to the plains; it also increases your chances of
successfully searching normally as well as giving you autosearching.
If you choose not to use Excalibur, I'd suggest Grayswandir. It deals
double damage and gets +d5 to hit against everything (whereas Fire
Brand gets no bonuses against fire-resistant monsters) And gets a nice
silver bonus against a lot of late-game enemies, including demons.


